claim.claim-text:
converting light input to respective photoelectric conversion elements (12) constituting a plurality of pixels (11) of a CMOS image sensor (10) to charge, wherein a readout noise of the CMOS image sensor (10) is equal to or less than 0.4 e-rms;
amplifying, by an amplifier (13) constituting the plurality of pixels (11), the converted charge and converting the charge to a voltage;
converting, by an A/D converter (15), the voltages output from the respective amplifiers (13) to digital values and outputting the digital values; and
converting the digital value of each of the plurality of pixels (11) output from the A/D converter (15) to the number of photons based on threshold value data for distinguishing between adjacent numbers of photons.
